    "summary_en": "Automated Python quantitative screening across 503 S&P 500 constituents combining FCF Yield, ROIC moats, aggressive share buybacks (Cannibals), SEC 10-Q RPO backlog surges, and Form 4 insider cluster buying.",
    "summary_kr": "S&P 500 전 종목(503개 기업)을 대상으로 FCF Yield, ROIC 경제적 해자, 연간 유통주식수 감소율(자사주 소각), SEC 10-Q 수주잔고(RPO) 급증 및 내부자 장내매수(Form 4)를 교차 검증한 파이썬 퀀트 리서치입니다.",
    "html": "<h3>1. Methodology &amp; Multi-Factor Screening Architecture</h3>\n<p>This quantitative equity research pipeline screens all <strong>503 S&amp;P 500 constituents</strong> using Python and SEC EDGAR XBRL filings across three orthogonal alpha tracks:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Track 1 (Valuation &amp; Drawdown Margin of Safety):</strong> Free Cash Flow (FCF) Yield &ge; 4.0% combined with a 52-Week High Drawdown &le; -15.0%.</li>\n  <li><strong>Track 2 (Economic Moat &amp; Share Cannibals):</strong> Return on Invested Capital (ROIC) &ge; 15.0% paired with aggressive net share count reduction (YoY Share Change &le; -3.0%).</li>\n  <li><strong>Track 3 (SEC XBRL RPO Inflection &amp; Form 4 Open-Market Insider Buying):</strong> Automated parsing of 10-Q Remaining Performance Obligations (RPO) / deferred revenue acceleration and Form 4 Code P open-market purchases by C-suite executives and institutional super-investors.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>2. Key Alpha Intersections (Track 1 &cap; Track 2 &cap; Track 3)</h3>\n<p>Six high-ROIC compounders simultaneously cleared the valuation drawdown filter (52W Drawdown &le; -15%, FCF Yield &ge; 4%) and the strict Share Cannibal threshold (YoY Shares &le; -3.0%):</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Uber Technologies (UBER):</strong> -31.27% off 52W high | <strong>7.11% FCF Yield</strong> ($5,078M H1 FCF, 97.4% cash conversion) | <strong>26.07% ROIC</strong> | <strong>-3.55% YoY share count reduction</strong> | Concurrent Form 4 Code P open-market purchases by CEO ($10.01M) and COO ($5.31M).</li>\n  <li><strong>Gartner (IT):</strong> #1 Share Cannibal in the S&amp;P 500 with <strong>-13.93% YoY share reduction</strong> | -29.26% drawdown | <strong>10.85% FCF Yield</strong> | <strong>21.04% ROIC</strong> | 16.86x P/E.</li>\n  <li><strong>Fair Isaac (FICO):</strong> <strong>73.93% ROIC</strong> | 53.79% operating margin (+485 bps YoY) | <strong>-7.62% YoY share reduction</strong> | 5.04% FCF Yield.</li>\n  <li><strong>Booking Holdings (BKNG), NVR (NVR) &amp; Otis Worldwide (OTIS):</strong> Sustained capital-light compounding with ROIC ranging from 24.5% to 80.0% and annual share buybacks between -3.1% and -8.4%.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>3. SEC 10-Q RPO Backlog Inflection &amp; AI Power Bottlenecks</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Comfort Systems USA (FIX):</strong> 49.56% ROIC, +50.26% YoY revenue growth, and <strong>+68.7% YoY same-store organic backlog expansion</strong> ($14.06B total backlog verified via SEC 10-Q).</li>\n  <li><strong>Caterpillar (CAT):</strong> 22.12% ROIC and <strong>$44.10B in long-term Remaining Performance Obligations (+123.86% YoY)</strong> driven by AI data center prime-power gas turbine demand.</li>\n</ul>"
