    "title": "NBA Player of the week? Potential MVPs?",
    "date_iso": "2018-11-20",
    "date_str": "November 20, 2018",
    "original_url": "https://dohyungchoi.wordpress.com/2018/11/20/nba-player-of-the-week-potential-mvps/",
    "thumb": "assets/posts/nba-player-of-the-week-potential-mvps/thumb.png",
    "fig_count": 5,
    "excerpt": "NBA player of the week awards are given to players who have performed well in the games in the week that they are awarded. It is said that more you win the player of the week title, it is an indication that you are a dom...",
    "word_count": 694,
    "read_time_min": 4,
    "html": "<p>NBA player of the week awards are given to players who have performed well in the games in the week that they are awarded. It is said that more you win the player of the week title, it is an indication that you are a dominant player in the league and it increases your chances of getting the seasonal MVP title.</p>\n<p>I looked at a dataset showing NBA player of the week from 1985 to 2017, to see which players were selected the most and at what age did players get the titles the most to assess the best performing ages for the basketball players. I also looked at whether player position (guard, forward or center) had influences in the title. The dataset can be downloaded from the link (<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/jacobbaruch/nba-player-of-the-week\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.kaggle.com/jacobbaruch/nba-player-of-the-week</a>)</p>\n<p><img class=\"alignnone  wp-image-111\" src=\"assets/posts/nba-player-of-the-week-potential-mvps/fig_1.png\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2018-12-16 at 7.36.43 PM\" width=\"298\" height=\"384\" /></p>\n<p>The above table shows the top 10 list of who received the most number of the player of the week titles from 1985 to 2017. You see familiar names like LeBron James, Kobe Bryant and Michael Jordan. All other players in this list are legendary players in the league and most of them have received season MVPs or final MVPs. This somewhat shows that the more players win the player of the week awards, it is likely they win the MVPs and become well-known legendary players in the basketball history.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-112\" src=\"assets/posts/nba-player-of-the-week-potential-mvps/fig_2.png\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2018-12-16 at 7.36.55 PM\" width=\"170\" height=\"216\" /></p>\n<p>The graph above shows at which age players received the title the most. The age ranges from 24 to 28. This corresponds to men&#8217;s prime physical age, and given that most players make a debut in the league in between 19 to 22, this means that players have higher chance of receiving the title when they are younger than 30. Another insight we can get from is that the best players from the first graph only needed few years to dominate the league. This might be a good reason for college scouts to really try hard to find potential NBA draftees that have higher chances of becoming great players in the NBA because once these players get drafted, they will soon start to dominate the games!</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-113\" src=\"assets/posts/nba-player-of-the-week-potential-mvps/fig_3.png\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2018-12-16 at 7.37.04 PM\" width=\"214\" height=\"187\" /></p>\n<p>During the draft period, basketball fans and commentators talk about whether a specific draft year has a good pool of potentials or not. Depending on these predictions, value of a draftee increases or decreases not only by the players participating in that specific draft year, but also players that participated the year before or that will participate in the year after. Therefore, it is important to see which year was the most &#8220;successful&#8221; draft year, and see whether there is a pattern. According to the data, 2003 NBA draft was the most successful draft. It had players like LeBron James (1st), Dwyane Wade (10th), and Carmelo Anthony (11st). Draftees from no particular draft year had this many number of NBA draftees at this high ranking. Year 1996 was successful with Allen Iverson and Kobe Bryant, and year 1984 with the one and only, Michael Jordan.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"alignnone  wp-image-90\" src=\"assets/posts/nba-player-of-the-week-potential-mvps/fig_4.png\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2018-11-20 at 11.37.37 PM\" width=\"279\" height=\"212\" /></p>\n<p>According to the above data, 40% of the players were guards, 38.5% forwards and 21.5% were centers. This shows that relatively smaller players (guards and forwards) in general have the higher chances of getting the awards. The average weight of the title winning centers are 261 pounds, forwards with 235 pounds and guards with 198 pounds. The combined insight from all of the above information enables to summarize that the players who will have the highest chances of winning the NBA player of the week are players who are:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>guards</li>\n<li>playing 4th or 5th season in the league</li>\n<li>weight around 200 to 210 pounds</li>\n</ol>\n<p>My prediction for a player who will win the most player of the week titles is..</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-91\" src=\"assets/posts/nba-player-of-the-week-potential-mvps/fig_5.png\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2018-11-20 at 11.45.20 PM\" /></p>\n<p>C.J Mccollum! He was drafted as a 10th pick in the first round in 2013. It&#8217;s been his fifth season in the NBA, and he weighs 197 pounds according to the official NBA profile. He is a guard player playing for the Portland Trail Blazers. Let&#8217;s see whether he will become one of the dominant players of NBA proven through the player of the week titles, and check whether one day he will be the MVP of the league as well!</p>",
